{
 "id": "ttl/mixed-dead-tail-read/hot-after-6-minutes",
 "description": "r0 sends a 1h mark on messages[1] and a 5m mark on messages[2]. The change shrinks messages[2] from 2,000 to 500 tokens, so the forwarded body is 5,500 tokens and r0 writes 5,500, of which 5,000 at 1h. r1 comes 6 minutes later: the 1h head is alive, the 5m tail is dead on the clock. The provider billed a read of all 5,500 tokens. The billed read proves the tail was alive, so the boundary is the end of messages[2] and the replayed 1,500 tokens are READ (1,500 x $0.30/M = $0.00045). Without the read rule the library stopped at the head and booked a 5m write (1,500 x $3.75/M).",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#40",
